{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-3185-76b5-8778-4348cba9fef2","id":"01a1a5e9-81c2-7710-8c46-54cc2b607b8e","idempotency_key":"a27ec2e39ba6bc4bd30f899bdf83ca8bddb68c928637a5823f02df8f6a2a0c3d","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T09:35:06Z","payload":{"note":"Watch mode. rbc-ai::play::watch_seats reads both seats from a match whose players are both models, and watch_step asks whoever is to move for one ply through the same validated driver the human-vs-AI path uses, so a watched game cannot record an illegal move. WatchSettings on MatchConfig carries white_reasoning/black_reasoning: request_reasoning follows the side's own toggle, and when it comes back the reasoning is written onto that ply with annotate_ply, which is what puts it in the PGN as a comment - so one side can be annotated and the other silent in the same game. Match::pause/resume/reset: a paused match refuses moves ('the game is paused'), resume restores awaiting_white/black from whose turn it is, and reset rebuilds from the config, dropping the record because a reset is a new game and keeping the plies would make the PGN a lie. Routes: POST /api/ai/matches/{id}/watch/step (plies 1..20, stopping at the end of the game or when a model cannot produce a legal move, keeping the plies already played), /watch/pause, /watch/resume, /watch/reset. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features --test watch -> 10 tests (both seats found and a mixed game refused, one ply per side, pause refuses and resume plays, pause twice and after the end, reset to the start, only the toggled side annotated, an unannotated ply ignored). Live: 2 plies stepped (a3, a6), pause answered changed:true and a step then answered 'the game is paused', resume to awaiting_white, reset to 0 plies. Browser: cdp_ai_watch.js -> AI_WATCH_PASS with plies [[a3,true],[a6,false]] and PGN '1. a3 {controls the centre} a6 *'. Note: there is no watch UI yet - that is t-f26f - so the browser check drives the routes from the page origin.","target":"t-1315"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
